theory.intro:
**Integers** are positive whole numbers, negative whole numbers, and zero. On a number line, consecutive integers are evenly spaced.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-5.2,0) -- (5.2,0);
\foreach \v in {-4,...,4} {\draw (\v,0.15) -- (\v,-0.15); \node[below] at (\v,-0.15) {$\v$};}
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.4,0.7) -- (-3.6,0.7);
\node[above] at (-2,0.85) {negative};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0.4,0.7) -- (3.6,0.7);
\node[above] at (2,0.85) {positive};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

